      },
      "note": "The php grammar (PHP with the HTML around it), not php_only. PHP runs only what sits inside <?php ... ?>; the rest of a .php file is output. The php grammar reads it that way: text outside the tags is a text node, and the PHP inside the tags gets the same syntax nodes php_only gives. php_only reads the whole file as code, so a template's HTML becomes syntax errors and prose outside any tag can become a dependency PHP never has. The whole PHP relation catalogue passes on both (test/relations/php-grammar.test.mjs pins the difference)."
